Darwin: every UBO of a Metal shader may be pushed; pushed words read in one copy.

A34 (local to this port; nothing here goes upstream). From HackiOS's Mali Metal driver ("pushubo",
MIT, Copyright 2026 Darwin on redwood contributors; github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel,
branch mtk, tools/mesa/panfrost-redwood-perf.patch), ported to Mesa 26.3 and extended:

- pan_shader.c: a shader of the Metal driver (nir->info.label "air") may have any UBO pushed,
  not only UBO 0. CoreAnimation's uniforms are in Metal buffers 1 and up, which upstream leaves
  as loads from memory for every pixel. REDWOOD_PAN_PUSHUBO=0 (the plug-in's rwm_pushubo=0)
  keeps upstream's rule for shaders compiled from then on.
- pan_cmdstream.c, panfrost_emit_const_buf, in a process drawing through Metal only: a pushed
  word may come from any UBO -- from the user buffer, which the Metal driver sets to its
  buffer's mapping alongside the buffer itself (air_metal.c), or from the resource's own
  mapping after its GPU writes are flushed and waited for. The words of a UBO are read in one
  copy of the span they cover (up to 4 KB) into ordinary memory: the mapping is write-combined,
  ~0.1 us a load (boot 0962: 4 KB read a word at a time in 109 us, 3 in malloc's memory).

With the buffer bound as itself as well (air_metal.c), the GPU reads what is not pushed from the
buffer, and panfrost no longer copies a user buffer's whole range into the batch for every draw
-- the "ubos" step, ~360 us of a ~400 us draw in boot 0962.

